{
  "_comment": [
    "wave13 - three hostile monsters cut from Art/NPC/monsters/new.",
    "",
    "'frames' is a CHECK, not an override: slice_wave13_sheets.py finds the figures by",
    "connected components and refuses to build if the count disagrees. Every number here",
    "was produced by that segmentation and then spot-checked against a full-resolution",
    "view of the sheet - which is how three of them were caught being wrong when they had",
    "been read off a contact sheet by eye (walk is 7 not 6, heavy_attack is 8 not 6,",
    "muscle_run is 8 not 6).",
    "",
    "targetBodyPx is a WORLD SIZE, because NPC art imports at PPU 64: 168px = 2.63 units,",
    "240px = 3.75, 288px = 4.5. The player dwarf is 1.797 for comparison, so all three are",
    "deliberately bigger than the player, as asked.",
    "",
    "chase draws from the RUN sheet on both barbols - that is the whole reason a chase",
    "reads as a chase. The dragon has only three sheets, so it takes the binder's fallback",
    "chain for cast/damage/death (chase->walk, damage->idle, death->idle) and leans on",
    "GrayscaleDeath to sell dying, exactly as the barbarian player class does."
  ],
